docs {
  # POST /api/sales/ — Create sale (minimal)
  
  Creates `Client` + `Sale` (atomic via `transaction.atomic()`) and returns Stripe checkout link. Requires `Authorization: Token {{token}}`. Source: `travels/views.py:94 SaleViewSet.post` + `travels/serializers.py:50 SaleSerializer` (`source="client.name"` nesting, `vip_code` writeOnly `CharField(10)`).
  
  No `vip_code` key here → `sale.vip_code=None` and subsequent `GET /api/sales/?stripe_code=` returns `vip_code:null`.
  
  ## Status codes
  
  - `201 Created` — success, sale created
  - `400 Bad Request` — missing/invalid FKs (see `post_create_invalid.bru`)
  - `401 Unauthorized` — invalid `vip_code` (see `post_create_invalid_vip_code.bru`), or missing/invalid token
  
  ## Response (201)
  
  ```json
  {
    "status": "success",
    "message": "Sale created successfully",
    "data": {
      "payment_link": "https://checkout.stripe.com/c/pay/..."
    }
  }
  ```
  
  `payment_link` is dynamic per sale (`utils/stripe.py:42` → external `STRIPE_API_HOST`), only prefix `https://checkout.stripe.com/` is assertable. `total` is derived from `Pricing` per `serializers.py:97` (example `80.00` One Way Lux SUV at Alegranza, `160.00` Round Trip).
  
  ## Error (400) — missing fields
  
  ```json
  {
    "status": "error",
    "message": "Invalid sale data",
    "errors": {
      "service_type": ["Este campo es requerido."],
      "client_name": ["Este campo es requerido."],
      "client_email": ["Este campo es requerido."],
      "location": ["Este campo es requerido."],
      "vehicle": ["Este campo es requerido."]
    }
  }
  ```
  
  ## Notes
  
  - `client_last_name` is optional here (see `post_create_full.bru`).
  - `vip_code` omitted → `null` (see `post_create_empty_vip_code.bru` for explicit `""`/`null`).
}
